class.description:
A [ResourceLocalizationCatalog] maps the path of a resource (the key) to its localized path per locale, for example [code]res://voice/intro.ogg[/code] to [code]res://voice/de/intro.ogg[/code] in [code]"de"[/code]. Each key can name the resource type it expects. See [LocalizationCatalog] for the file formats; in CSV the expected type is the [code]?type[/code] column, in the other formats the [code]_type[/code] field.
It holds the same data as the project setting [code]internationalization/locale/translation_remaps[/code]; [method add_translation_remaps] and [method to_translation_remaps] convert between both.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var catalog = ResourceLocalizationCatalog.new()
catalog.set_localized_path("res://voice/intro.ogg", "de", "res://voice/de/intro.ogg")
catalog.set_expected_type("res://voice/intro.ogg", &"AudioStream")
print(catalog.to_translation_remaps()) # { "res://voice/intro.ogg": ["res://voice/de/intro.ogg:de"] }
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var catalog = new ResourceLocalizationCatalog();
catalog.SetLocalizedPath("res://voice/intro.ogg", "de", "res://voice/de/intro.ogg");
catalog.SetExpectedType("res://voice/intro.ogg", "AudioStream");
GD.Print(catalog.ToTranslationRemaps());
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
